# Pro Git - A Comprehensive Guide to Using Git on the command line

Here's a guide to Pro Git and learning Git on the command line so that you can become a Git pro. 

Git is a powerful tool which, with the right learning, can solve many of your coding problems. This guide is designed to give you a good understanding of the Git commands and how to use them most effectively. If you're looking for a basic understanding, then go through the section 'Chapter 1: Getting Started'.

This guide will cover:

- Creating and configuring a Git Repository
- Recording changes to the repository
- Viewing the commit--------------------            Debug.Assert((New_arrListIndexOfX == -1 ? true : false));

